WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:16.000
SoherAgent explores how software agents can move from a request to reviewable work, with a person deciding what is accepted.

2
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Generating code is one step. A useful development workflow also needs shared context, ownership and a way to judge the result.

3
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:48.000
For example, a team wants an internal tool to understand service contracts. Agree what it should do and which information it may use.

4
00:00:48.000 --> 00:01:04.000
A coordinating agent holds the plan. Other agents take on specific tasks and bring their results back for review.

5
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:20.000
You choose the scope and the tools. The agent works within those limits and brings decisions back to your team.

6
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:36.000
Possible starting points include an internal tool, a connection between systems or a focused change to existing software.

7
00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:52.000
The agent presents the proposed change and any open questions. Your team reviews the result before accepting it.

8
00:01:52.000 --> 00:02:08.000
We can scope an engineering-agent workflow around your tools, permissions and review process. The first conversation starts with the work your team needs to do.
